WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.540
Hey guys, it's officially less than 100 days till election day, so I just wanted to hop

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.980
on here to give a basic breakdown of what's at stake nationally this November.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.220
2026 is a midterm election year, just meaning that it happens at the midway point of a president's

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.060
time in office, but it is super important because it holds the possibility of flipping

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.980
the majority party in Congress and in the Senate, which will set the tone for the remainder of a

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.140
president's time in office. Right now, Republicans hold the majority in both chambers of Congress,

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.060
which allows Trump and his administration to enact their agenda in a way that would not be

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.180
possible in a divided Congress. Because briefly stated, the party that holds the

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.740
majority shapes the direction of policy and holds control over the legislative

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.260
process. That's what makes midterm elections so important because during

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.660
midterm years all 435 seats of the House are up for re-election as well as the

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.980
regular one-third of Senate seats. What that means for this upcoming November is

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.780
Democrats have the chance to flip the House and the Senate which would make it

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.100
a lot more difficult for President Trump to make progress in his agenda. I

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.580
cannot overstate how important this is. We are in a pivotal time in history and

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.100
and flipping the House and the Senate is the most important thing we can do right now.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:05.540
So please get out and vote. It really comes down to just upholding the principles of democracy,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:11.860
so please do what you can, get involved, and like I already said, vote. That's all she wrote, bye guys!
